WEBVTT

00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:12.305
Get the word out to Remus and the others
that Harry's back.

00:00:12.347 --> 00:00:14.641
Okay, let's not kill him before
You-Know-Who--

00:00:14.683 --> 00:00:16.351
River, D.A. calling. Do you read?

00:00:16.393 --> 00:00:18.311
We have a new weather report:
Lightning has struck.

00:00:20.397 --> 00:00:21.273
What's the plan, Harry?

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:27.153
HARRY:
Okay.

00:00:28.113 --> 00:00:30.365
There's something we need to find.

00:00:30.407 --> 00:00:35.495
Something hidden here in the castle.
And it may help us defeat You-Know-Who.

00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:37.455
Right. What is it?

00:00:37.497 --> 00:00:38.665
We don't know.

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:43.545
NEVILLE: Where is it?
HARRY: We don't know that either.

00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:48.258
-I realize it's not much to go on.
-That's nothing to go on.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.927
I think it has something to do
with Ravenclaw.

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:55.640
Um, it'll be small, easily concealed.

00:00:56.474 --> 00:00:58.643
Anyone, any ideas?

00:00:59.978 --> 00:01:02.606
Well, there's Rowena Ravenclaw's
lost diadem.

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:06.192
-Oh, bloody hell. Here we go.
LUNA: Lost diadem of Ravenclaw?

00:01:08.278 --> 00:01:11.823
Hasn't anyone heard of it?
It's quite famous.

00:01:11.865 --> 00:01:15.368
Yes, but, Luna, it's lost,
for centuries now.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.330
There isn't a person alive today
who's seen it.

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:20.707
Excuse me. Can someone tell me
what a bloody diadem is?

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:23.501
It's a sort of crown.
You know, like a tiara.

00:01:24.002 --> 00:01:25.754
[RUMBLING]

00:01:26.755 --> 00:01:28.006
Harry.

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:30.592
Hi there.

00:01:33.762 --> 00:01:36.973
Six months she hasn't seen me
and it's like I'm Frankie First-Year.

00:01:37.015 --> 00:01:38.892
-I'm her brother.
-Got lots of those.

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:41.353
-There's only one Harry.
-Shut up, Seamus.

00:01:41.394 --> 00:01:43.021
What is it, Ginny?

00:01:43.063 --> 00:01:47.275
Snape knows. He knows that Harry
was spotted in Hogsmeade.

00:01:51.112 --> 00:01:53.698
[GROUP MARCHING]

00:02:26.523 --> 00:02:31.903
Many of you are surely wondering
why I have summoned you at this hour.

00:02:34.364 --> 00:02:38.118
It's come to my attention
that earlier this evening...

00:02:39.577 --> 00:02:41.955
...Harry Potter was sighted
in Hogsmeade.

00:02:41.996 --> 00:02:43.998
[MURMURING]

00:02:44.332 --> 00:02:46.042
Now...

00:02:46.084 --> 00:02:47.711
...should anyone...

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:54.592
...student or staff,
attempt to aid Mr. Potter...

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.012
...they will be punished...

00:02:58.054 --> 00:03:02.642
...in a manner consistent with
the severity of their transgression.

00:03:02.684 --> 00:03:04.936
Furthermore...

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:09.941
...any person found to have knowledge
of these events...

00:03:11.276 --> 00:03:15.238
...who fails to come forward...

00:03:16.156 --> 00:03:20.744
...will be treated as...

00:03:21.411 --> 00:03:24.622
...equally guilty.

00:03:26.916 --> 00:03:28.752
Now then...

00:03:32.213 --> 00:03:34.299
...if anyone here...

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:40.972
...has any knowledge of Mr. Potter's
movements this evening...

00:03:43.183 --> 00:03:47.061
...I invite them to step forward...

00:03:50.607 --> 00:03:52.317
...now.

00:04:02.827 --> 00:04:04.829
[MURMURING]

00:04:06.956 --> 00:04:10.960
It seems, despite your exhaustive
defensive strategies...

00:04:11.002 --> 00:04:13.671
...you still have a bit of a security problem,
headmaster.

00:04:17.175 --> 00:04:20.178
And I'm afraid it's quite extensive.

00:04:20.929 --> 00:04:23.014
How dare you stand where he stood?

00:04:24.641 --> 00:04:26.893
Tell them how it happened that night.

00:04:26.935 --> 00:04:31.481
Tell them how you looked him in the eye,
a man who trusted you, and killed him.

00:04:31.856 --> 00:04:33.525
Tell them.

00:04:51.668 --> 00:04:52.794
[WIZARDS GRUNT]

00:04:58.383 --> 00:04:59.384
McGONAGALL:
Coward!

00:05:02.345 --> 00:05:04.848
[STUDENTS CHEERING]

00:05:08.476 --> 00:05:10.937
VOLDEMORT:
Harry.

00:05:12.063 --> 00:05:13.231
McGONAGALL:
Potter?

00:05:23.032 --> 00:05:25.201
[RUMBLING]

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.417
[GIRL 1 SCREAMING]

00:05:36.713 --> 00:05:38.882
[GIRL 2 SCREAMING]

00:05:43.094 --> 00:05:45.430
[GIRL 3 SCREAMING]

00:05:47.891 --> 00:05:53.563
VOLDEMORT:
I know that many of you will want to fight.

00:05:53.605 --> 00:05:58.651
Some of you may even think
that to fight is wise.

00:05:59.068 --> 00:06:02.113
But this is folly.

00:06:02.614 --> 00:06:05.450
Give me Harry Potter.

00:06:06.409 --> 00:06:10.705
Do this and none shall be harmed.

00:06:10.747 --> 00:06:16.920
Give me Harry Potter
and I shall leave Hogwarts untouched.

00:06:16.961 --> 00:06:20.006
Give me Harry Potter...

00:06:20.048 --> 00:06:24.093
...and you will be rewarded.

00:06:24.135 --> 00:06:27.764
You have one hour.

